{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Viewport-Width Client Hint.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Viewport-Width Client Hint.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"viewport width client hint viewport width client hint","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Viewport-Width Client Hint.md","fileName":"Viewport-Width Client Hint.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Viewport-Width Client Hint","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-28 04:01\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching","Resource Width Client Hint","highperformanceimages.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Viewport-Width Client Hint.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Viewport-Width Client Hint.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"viewport width client hint viewport width client hint","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Viewport-Width Client Hint.md","fileName":"Viewport-Width Client Hint.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Viewport-Width Client Hint","heading":"Viewport-Width Client Hint","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Viewport-Width hint communicates the width of the client’s layout viewport in CSS pixels. An image service can use it to place the request into a coarse responsive breakpoint when markup does not enumerate candidates.\n\nViewport width alone does not reveal the actual image slot or required physical pixels. Layout can allocate only part of the viewport, and device density changes the sample requirement. It should therefore be combined with resource width or a conservative layout model. See [[Resource Width Client Hint]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching","Resource Width Client Hint","highperformanceimages.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF